   "name": "Le Chapiteau du Cirque",
   "room_id": "R_adv_manner_01",
   "image": "cirque/cirque.jpg",
   "alt": "Inside the red-and-white striped big top, painted in ink and gouache, under bunting and string lights, with a Ferris wheel in the park outside the open tent flap at the far left. High up a ringmistress cracks her whip as a little flower meadow bursts from the sawdust, a girl on one leg balances a strawberry parfait and a poodle hugs a black boot. On the red pedestal a strongman lifts a dewy rose gently, another lifts a baby elephant, a seal claps and a clown's teapot lid pops off on a drum. In the ring a clown zips by on a unicycle, a vet rushes to a seal, a clown's shopping bags burst and a blindfolded clown walks into a cream pie. At the ring's edge a clown springs out of a trapdoor, a little ghost makes the crowd jump up, a lion naps in a wooden boat, clowns climb aboard a red wagon and a troupe squeezes into a tiny striped car. A red-curtained arch with a clown sign on the left and a green-curtained arch on the right lead to other rooms, with curtained doorways on the balconies above; a striped ticket booth stands at the right.",
