   "alt": "The clowns' practice ring inside the red-and-white striped big top, painted in ink and gouache under strings of lights, seen from the edge of the sawdust ring. At the back a man in a toga juggles freely above a brass balance, a swan balances an egg on its head and a clown saws at his viola so violently that his hat flies off. A girl waves a red flag, a seal raises its flipper with a ball on its nose while a clown holds up a hoop, and a puppy watches from the door of a little striped tent. In the ring a white-faced mime tiptoes silently, three seals balance beach balls and a gray elephant edges along a low rope. At the front a polka-dot clown hides a cream pie behind his back while the ringmaster looks away, a coach in a tracksuit blows his whistle at a clown doing press-ups and a kind clown holds his umbrella over a granny with a cane. A big open steamer trunk spills costumes and props on the right. The red-curtained doorway on the left leads back to the big ring.",
